# Design System to Storybook

Use `skills/design-system-to-storybook/SKILL.md` when implementing Storybook foundations, shared UI components, and stories from an extracted design-system package.

## Source Of Truth

- Read `design-system/SESSION_STATE.md`.
- Read `design-system/COMPONENT_INVENTORY.md`.
- Read relevant `design-system/components/*.md`.
- Read `design-system/DESIGN_EVIDENCE_MAP.md` for evidence and source trace.
- Read touched token files under `tokens/`.
- Run `<skill-root>/scripts/trace_sources.mjs` and `<skill-root>/scripts/plan_component_batches.mjs` before multi-component implementation.
- Do not infer component design from screenshots or broad Figma search inside this workflow.

## Batch Rules

- Implement one bounded pass at a time.
- Default pass size is foundations only, 3-5 simple components, or 1-2 complex composites.
- If implementing more than one component, create or update `design-system/STORYBOOK_COMPONENT_PLAN.md` and `design-system/STORYBOOK_COMPONENT_QUEUE.md`.
- Update `design-system/STORYBOOK_IMPLEMENTATION_MAP.md` before code edits.
- Stop after verification and checkpoint update.

## Component Rules

- Resolve source trace before implementation.
- Implement components and pages with co-located stories unless existing product convention requires otherwise.
- Prefer reuse or extension of existing product components.
- Keep all visual values token-backed.
- Structure the rendered Storybook DOM for Figma export: stable visible root, `data-component`, variant/state markers, stable class prefixes, and token CSS variables.
- Add Storybook stories for documented variants and states.
- Mark missing specs as `needs-extraction`; do not invent undocumented variants.

## Figma Export Addon

For React Storybook 10 projects, install and configure the bundled addon with the skill scripts:

```sh
node <skill-root>/scripts/inspect_storybook_project.mjs <product-repo-root> --json
node <skill-root>/scripts/install_figma_export_addon.mjs <product-repo-root>
node <skill-root>/scripts/generate_figma_export_config.mjs <design-system-package-root> --product-root <product-repo-root> --write
node <skill-root>/scripts/generate_component_spec_modules.mjs <design-system-package-root> --product-root <product-repo-root> --write
node <skill-root>/scripts/sync_story_source_parameters.mjs <design-system-package-root> --product-root <product-repo-root> --write
node <skill-root>/scripts/validate_figma_export_setup.mjs <product-repo-root>
```

Configure `createFigmaExportReviewDecorator`, `review.css`, and `getFigmaSourceUrl` by default so review/Open source works. For stories, prefer `parameters.figmaSourceUrl` for Figma sources and `parameters.design.url` for other web sources from `STORYBOOK_SOURCE_TRACE.md`. Verify the toolbar, review/Open source overlay, and Copy design SVG action before marking addon setup complete.

Record Figma export structure decisions and exceptions in the implementation map. Do not mark a component/page done when its design source is only anonymous DOM, hashed classes, pseudo-element-only content, canvas-only rendering, or unresolved runtime animation state.
